g out of 1,200 Australian maritime jobs. We are an island nation. We have the fifth largest sea-bearing transport in the world. That mob over there want to deregister Australian ships. That is what this legislation will do. They want to do away with Australian jobs. There will be foreign seafarers on these vessels. It is a terrible piece of legislation, and I hope that the crossbenchers are well and truly across what the government are proposing to do, with this legislation. Gavin Marshall The question is that the Senate Rural and Regional Affairs and Transport Legislation Committee inquiry into the Shipping Legislation Amendment Bill 2015 be extended from 12 October until 19 October 2015.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-3936","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2015-10-12/3"}
